[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Starlark for .NET - host interface
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Draft, Active, Implemented, Open)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[FREETEXT]
How a running .NET program (the host) embeds the interpreter and exchanges data and control with Starlark scripts. The
host runs in-process. The comparable Rust interface is Evaluator, Module and the starlark_module macro. VERIFICATION
names the xunit test that covers a requirement. STATUS Open marks work that is not done yet.
[/FREETEXT]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Registering host functions and values

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-REG-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Typed function registration
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall let the host register a .NET delegate as a predeclared Starlark function, converting positional
and named arguments to the delegate's parameter types and converting the result back, without hand-written argument
handling.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.TypedFunctionsNeedNoArgumentHandling

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-REG-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Parameter naming and defaults
STATEMENT: >>>
A registered function shall accept each parameter by its declared name or its snake_case form, shall honour C# default
values for omitted parameters, and shall report a missing, unexpected, duplicate or excess argument as a Starlark error
that names the parameter.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.WrongArgumentTypesAreScriptErrors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-REG-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Predeclared values
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall let the host predeclare any .NET value as a global visible to every module, converted by the
value-mapping rules.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.ObjectsBecomeStructsWithSnakeCaseFields

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-REG-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Exposing a host object
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall let the host expose an object as a struct whose public properties are fields (a snapshot) and
whose public methods are live calls on that object, using snake_case names by default.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.ExposedObjectsGetLiveMethods

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-REG-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Host-defined script-visible types
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall let the host define a named value type with its own operators, attributes, methods, equality,
hashing and truthiness, so that it behaves as a built-in does (the Rust StarlarkValue trait).
<<<
VERIFICATION: HostValueTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-REG-006
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Opt-in exposure by attribute
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to mark which properties and methods of a class are visible to scripts, and members not marked
shall be invisible.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Value mapping

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: .NET to Starlark
STATEMENT: >>>
Conversion to Starlark shall map null to None, bool to bool, every integer type to int, float, double and decimal to
float, string and char to str, enums to their names, byte arrays to bytes, dictionaries to dict, other sequences to
list, value tuples to tuple, and delegates to callable functions. Any other object shall become a struct of its public
readable properties, converted recursively.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.NullablesAndPrimitivesRoundTrip

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Starlark to .NET
STATEMENT: >>>
Conversion from Starlark shall produce a requested .NET type, including nullable types, enums, arrays, lists, sets,
dictionaries, and classes or records bound by constructor and settable property from a struct, record or string-keyed
dict, matching the exact name or the snake_case form.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.ScriptValuesBindToRecordsAndClasses

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Range-checked integers
STATEMENT: >>>
Converting a Starlark int to a fixed-width .NET integer type shall fail with a Starlark error when the value does not
fit, and shall not wrap or throw a CLR exception.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.WrongArgumentTypesAreScriptErrors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Mismatches are Starlark errors
STATEMENT: >>>
A value that cannot be represented as the requested type, including None for a non-nullable value type and a missing
required field, shall raise a StarlarkException naming the Starlark type and the .NET type or field.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.MissingFieldsAreReported

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Cyclic host objects
STATEMENT: >>>
Converting a cyclic or excessively deep .NET object graph shall fail with a Starlark error and shall not overflow the
stack.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.CyclicObjectsAreRejectedNotLooped

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Host objects are snapshots and read-only to scripts
STATEMENT: >>>
A script shall not be able to modify a host object through a converted value. Changes the host makes after conversion
shall not be visible to the script unless it is converted again.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.ScriptsCannotChangeTheHostObject

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-MAP-007
STATUS: Open
TITLE: JSON shortcuts
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to pass a value to and from a script as JSON with one call each way, using the same field naming
as the struct mapping.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Running scripts and reading results

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-RUN-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Execute and read globals
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to execute source text or a parsed module and read the resulting global bindings by name.
<<<
VERIFICATION: EvalTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-RUN-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Call script functions from the host
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to call a global script function by name with .NET arguments and receive a .NET result of a
requested type.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.CallingScriptFunctionsFromTheHost

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-RUN-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Module loading
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall control what load() can read through a loader callback. An unknown module and a load cycle shall be
script errors.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-RUN-004
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Per-run host context
STATEMENT: >>>
A registered function shall be able to receive host state for the current run, the analogue of Evaluator.extra, without
capturing it in a closure, so one registered function can serve many runs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-RUN-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Asynchronous host functions
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to register a function returning Task, and a script shall be able to call it as if it were
synchronous, with cancellation honoured.
<<<
VERIFICATION: AsyncHostTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-RUN-006
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Shareable frozen modules
STATEMENT: >>>
A module that has been loaded and frozen shall be callable from many threads at once without data races.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Errors and diagnostics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-ERR-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Distinct failure kinds
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to tell apart a syntax error (StarlarkSyntaxException), a runtime error (StarlarkException), a
resource limit (ExecutionLimitException) and cancellation (OperationCanceledException). A script shall not be able to
catch the last two.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExecutionLimitTests.LimitIsNotAScriptError

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-ERR-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Source locations
STATEMENT: >>>
Script errors shall carry the file, line, column and a snippet of the offending source, and shall also provide the bare
message without the snippet.
<<<
VERIFICATION: TypeCheckerTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-ERR-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Host exceptions
STATEMENT: >>>
An exception thrown by a registered .NET function shall surface as a Starlark error naming the function. Limit and
cancellation exceptions shall pass through unchanged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: InteropTests.HostExceptionsBecomeScriptErrorsAndLimitsPassThrough

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-ERR-004
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Script call stack
STATEMENT: >>>
A runtime error shall include the chain of script function calls (file, line, function) that led to it, available to the
host as structured data.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Safety for untrusted scripts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-SAFE-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Step limit
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to cap the number of statements and expressions a run evaluates. Exceeding the cap shall raise
ExecutionLimitException, and the cap shall cover modules loaded during the run.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExecutionLimitTests.StepLimitStopsALongLoop

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-SAFE-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Time limit and cancellation
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to cap wall-clock time and pass a CancellationToken. A running script shall stop promptly when
either triggers.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExecutionLimitTests.TimeoutStopsALongLoop

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-SAFE-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Bounded call depth
STATEMENT: >>>
Deep or unbounded recursion shall fail with a Starlark error and shall not crash the process.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests.03_recursion_is_an_error

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-SAFE-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Memory limit
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to cap the memory a run may allocate, for example by bounding the size of collections, strings
and ranges that a script can build.
<<<
VERIFICATION: MemoryLimitTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-SAFE-005
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Capability listing
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to list every name visible to a script before the run, so the exposed surface can be reviewed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-SAFE-006
STATUS: Open
TITLE: No ambient authority
STATEMENT: >>>
With no host registrations, a script shall have no access to the file system, network, environment, clock or process.
A test shall enumerate the default universe to prove it.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Static checking

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-CHK-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Check before run
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to type check a module without running it, and to refuse to run a module that fails the check.
<<<
VERIFICATION: TypeCheckerTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HOST-CHK-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Checker knows host registrations
STATEMENT: >>>
The static checker shall use the .NET signatures of registered functions, exposed objects and predeclared values, so a
call with a wrong argument type is reported before the run.
<<<
COMMENT: The checker now follows load() into host-supplied modules (TypecheckLoadTests), but registered functions are still typed typing.Any.

[/SECTION]
